{
    "background_story": "Magnus was a majestic bird of paradise, renowned for his extravagant plumage. His feathers were a kaleidoscope of colors, with delicate plumes that resembled the finest silk. Magnus's most striking feature, however, was his magnificent tail, adorned with long, slender feathers that shimmered like jewels in the sunlight. During courtship season, Magnus would perform an elaborate dance, spreading his resplendent tail feathers like a fan and vibrating them with a soft humming noise. His plumelike adornments were not just for show; they also played a crucial role in attracting a mate and defending his territory from rival birds. Magnus's breathtaking beauty and impressive courtship displays made him the envy of the avian world, earning him the title of 'King of the Forest'.",
